From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: prospero-win <prospero-win@invalid>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 09:21:27 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: Run a write-watched write beside a protected page
 again only when its host page is writable.

A write to a write-watched page clears the watch on its host page and
is run again when the host page is writable now. That was judged by
the union of its pages' protections. With 16 KiB host pages and a
read-only or inaccessible page in the same host page (patch 0974), the
host page stays without write access, so the write faulted again, was
run again, and so on forever, the program seeing nothing. The Mario
Kart World PC port, which keeps its guest memory write-watched and
makes code pages read-only, hung on the PS5 at about 180,000 faults a
second on one page.

The host page protection Wine actually set now decides. When it is
still not writable, the fault goes on to the step over the neighbour
that other writes beside a protected page already take.
---
 dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
index 5c6e1013f3..24ff50c9c2 100644
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
@@ -5425,8 +5425,9 @@ NTSTATUS virtual_handle_fault( struct thread_data *data, EXCEPTION_RECORD *rec,
                 mprotect_range( page, host_page_size, 0, 0 );
             }
         }
-        /* ignore fault if page is writable now */
-        if (get_unix_prot( get_host_page_vprot( page )) & PROT_WRITE)
+        /* ignore fault if the host page is writable now: not only by the union of its
+         * pages, which a read-only or inaccessible neighbour can keep from it */
+        if (get_host_page_unix_prot( page, NULL, NULL, 0, 0 ) & PROT_WRITE)
         {
             if ((vprot & VPROT_WRITEWATCH) || is_write_watch_range( page, 1 ))
                 ret = STATUS_SUCCESS;
